# Both are optional. Leave them unset for local development.
#
# The Vite dev server proxies /api and /auth to the gateway (see vite.config.ts),
# so the browser makes same-origin requests and no CORS configuration is needed.
# Set these only when the API is not reachable at the same origin as the app -
# a deployed build served from somewhere other than the dev server, for example.
#
# Be aware: pointing these at a different origin means the browser will start
# preflighting requests, and the gateway does not answer preflights today. It
# treats /api/** as secured, and a preflight carries no Authorization header, so
# AuthenticationFilter rejects it with 401 before the real request is sent.
# Using these therefore also requires CORS support on the gateway, which does
# not exist yet.

# VITE_API_URL=https://your-gateway.example.com/api
# VITE_AUTH_URL=https://your-gateway.example.com/auth
